# Hunch account access: isolated fiction never calls Privy or sends email.
fold folded
rotate portrait
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.hunch
shell am start -n dev.omalauncher.hunch/.MainActivity --es authFixture demo
expect FICTIONAL SIGN-IN DEMO
expect Start with email
shot hunch-auth-start
# Invalid input never advances to OTP or account.
tap Send email code
expect Enter a valid email address
tap Email address
type demo@example.invalid
key BACK
tap Send email code
expect Code sent to demo@example.invalid
shot hunch-auth-code
rotate landscape
expect Code sent to demo@example.invalid
rotate portrait
expect Code sent to demo@example.invalid
tap Email code
type 999999
key BACK
tap Verify email code
expect That code could not be verified
tap Email code
type 123456
key BACK
tap Verify email code
expect Recovery email: demo@example.invalid
scrollto Your email login stays available for recovery
expect Your email login stays available for recovery
shot hunch-auth-add-passkey
scrollto Add a passkey
tap Add a passkey
expect Passkey added
expect Recovery email: demo@example.invalid
shot hunch-auth-linked
scrollto Sign out
tap Sign out
expect Start with email
scrollto Sign in with an existing passkey
tap Sign in with an existing passkey
expect Passkey sign-in did not complete
expect Start with email
fold open
rotate portrait
expect Sign in to Hunch
shot hunch-auth-inner
key BACK
expect "Today's issue"
# Leave live market mode. No email/credential activity is automatically started.
shell am force-stop dev.omalauncher.hunch
shell am start -n dev.omalauncher.hunch/.MainActivity
expect "Today's issue"
[phone] Owner explicitly sends own email code, enters it, adds passkey with Credential Manager, cancels once then completes, signs out and signs back in with passkey. Verify recovery email remains linked after restart. Check network failure and cover/unfold transitions without duplicate sends. Real domain must match installed phone signer. No wallet, deposits, orders or signatures.
